From: dArkOS RG52 Mini port
Subject: GammaOS's GPU timer only when asked for

GammaOS's azahar-nano measures GPU time per kind of work
(vk_gammaos_gpu_timer.h): a pair of timestamps around every render pass,
clear, blit, copy, upload and the present, read back three frames later.
It started on the first frame whenever the GPU has timestamps, so every
game paid for it on every frame, while only a profiling session reads the
sums. A timestamp after a pass waits for that pass's work, and malisx2 turns
each one into a job barrier.

Now it starts only with persist.gammaos.azahar_nano.gputime=1 (on Linux the
environment variable persist_gammaos_azahar_nano_gputime=1).

Castlevania: Lords of Shadow - Mirror of Fate on the RG52 Mini, frames 360
to 660 of the intro, GPU job slots traced in kbase: on libmali 50.1 ms a
frame before, 48.7 after (vertex-slot jobs 86 a frame before, 40 after); on
malisx2 64.0 before, 63.1 after.

--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_gammaos_gpu_timer.h
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_gammaos_gpu_timer.h
@@ -42,6 +42,7 @@
     std::uint32_t frame = 0;   // index of the pool being recorded
     double period_ns = 1.0;
     bool enabled = false;
+    bool checked = false;  // dArkOS: whether the switch below was read
     bool presenting = false;
     // accumulated over the trace window, in ms
     std::array<double, NumCategories> sum_ms{};
@@ -53,6 +54,15 @@
 
 inline State g;
 
+// dArkOS: the timer runs only with persist.gammaos.azahar_nano.gputime=1 (on Linux the
+// variable persist_gammaos_azahar_nano_gputime). Every pair of timestamps orders the GPU
+// work around it (malisx2 turns each into a job barrier), and only a profiling session
+// reads the sums.
+inline bool Wanted() {
+    char v[PROP_VALUE_MAX] = {};
+    return __system_property_get("persist.gammaos.azahar_nano.gputime", v) > 0 && v[0] == '1';
+}
+
 inline void Init(vk::Device device, float timestamp_period_ns, bool supported) {
     if (!supported || g.enabled) return;
     g.device = device;
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/renderer_vulkan.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/renderer_vulkan.cpp
@@ -1655,10 +1655,13 @@
     g_swap_trace.last = trace_t0;
     g_swap_trace.last_cpu_ms = trace_cpu;
 #endif
-    if (!GammaGpu::g.enabled) {
-        const auto props = instance.GetPhysicalDevice().getProperties();
-        GammaGpu::Init(instance.GetDevice(), props.limits.timestampPeriod,
-                       props.limits.timestampComputeAndGraphics);
+    if (!GammaGpu::g.enabled && !GammaGpu::g.checked) {
+        GammaGpu::g.checked = true;
+        if (GammaGpu::Wanted()) {
+            const auto props = instance.GetPhysicalDevice().getProperties();
+            GammaGpu::Init(instance.GetDevice(), props.limits.timestampPeriod,
+                           props.limits.timestampComputeAndGraphics);
+        }
     }
     GammaGpu::FrameBoundary();
     renderpass_cache.EndRendering();
